  "question": {
    "text": "A flat mirror revolves at a constant angular velocity making <math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></math> revolutions per second. With what velocity (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)&nbsp;will a light spot move along a spherical screen with a radius of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, if the mirror is at the centre of curvature of the screen?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>37.7</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>60.3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>68.7</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>75.4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> Angular velocity of the mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Angular velocity of the reflected ray<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ra</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Hence, the velocity of light spot over the screen<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75.4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"
  }
